{"term":"shore","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:7291c323f477491ab0","definition":"Land adjoining a non-flowing body of water, such as an ocean, lake or pond.","example":"lake shore; bay shore; gulf shore; island shore; mainland shore; river shore; estuary shore; pond shore; sandy shore; rocky shore","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["longshoreman","shorage"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shore#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5a0b3609cfe527502b","definition":"Land, usually near a port.","example":"The seamen were serving on shore instead of on ships.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["longshoreman","shorage"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shore#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f92b872ae55f286c43","definition":"To arrive at the shore","example":"the ship quickened her way, and shot past that rocke, where wee thought shee would have shored.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"intransitive, obsolete","wordFamily":["longshoreman","shorage"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shore#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:05dacbc4591800573a","definition":"To put ashore.","example":"I will bring these two moles, these blind ones, aboard him: if he think it fit to shore them again","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["longshoreman","shorage"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikti